meta_review.text:
Build in the controls that would falsify the mechanism:
- a matched-rate anti-targeted arm;
- noise-norm matching, so arms differ only in which tokens are dropped;
- an epochs-tuned or cosine-decay/early-stopping reference for the early-stopping explanation, rather than just reporting the peak epoch.
When targeting tokens, prefer static, model-independent rankings (chi-square, PMI) over self-refreshing gradient saliency, which can feed back on itself.
